-- title:
--   Theorem F: for z rational in u with |u|² algebraic, which conjugation hulls span(1, u, ū, z, z̄) carry a 2×3 configuration
-- statement:
--   Let $u \in \mathbb{C}$ be transcendental, that is, $u \notin \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the algebraic numbers); spans and linear independence are over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Suppose $u\bar u$ is algebraic, let $z$ lie in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(u)$, the subfield of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $u$, and let $W_z = \mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u, z, \bar z)$, the conjugation hull of $z$. Then $W_z$ carries a $2 \times 3$ configuration (linearly independent $x_0, x_1 \in \mathbb{C}$ and linearly independent $y_0, y_1, y_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ with every $x_iy_j \in W_z$) if and only if one of the following holds:
--
--   - $\dim W_z = 4$, and $z \in \mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u, (u - a)^{-1})$ for some $a \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $a\bar a = u\bar u$;
--   - $\dim W_z = 5$, and $W_z$ satisfies (D1), (D2a) or (D2b) below.
--
--   Here, with $W = W_z$:
--
--   - **(D1)** there are linearly independent $t_0, t_1, t_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ with $t_j \in W$ and $ut_j \in W$ for every $j$;
--   - **(D2a, two-orbit)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), P'(u)S_2(u)/(uQ'(u)))$ for some $P', Q', S_1, S_2 \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[X]$ with $P', Q'$ coprime, $\max(\deg P', \deg Q') = 2$ and $\deg S_1, \deg S_2 \leq 2$;
--   - **(D2b, cyclic)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), Q'(u)(Q'(u)S_1(u) + P'(u)S_2(u))/(uP'(u)^2))$ for some such $P', Q', S_1, S_2$.
--
--   **Proof.** $W_z$ is spanned by five vectors and contains $\mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u)$, of dimension $3$ (a relation $a + bu + c\bar u = 0$ times $u$ is $c\rho + au + bu^2 = 0$ with $\rho = u\bar u \neq 0$ algebraic), so $\dim W_z \in \{3, 4, 5\}$. In dimension $3$, $W_z = \mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u)$, and a $2 \times 3$ configuration there contradicts `DiazModulus.circle_point_config_card_le_four` ($2 + 3 > 4$). In dimension $4$ the equivalence is `DiazModulus.conj_hull_finrank_four_two_by_three_configuration_iff`. In dimension $5$, `DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_le_adjoin` gives $u^{-1} \in W_z$ and $W_z \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}(u)$, so `DiazModulus.rational_space_two_by_three_configuration_iff` applies to $W = W_z$. Both directions follow.
--
--   **Novelty.** Not found in the sources read: the “only if” half, the classification. Theorem F asks the question of Theorem E of the mission's research note (the Laurent case, formal as `DiazModulus.laurent_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff`) for every $z$ rational in $u$, and builds on Theorem B (`DiazModulus.circle_point_extension_two_by_three_configuration_iff`, 10.6), which holds for every complex $z$. For Laurent $z$, that its answer gives back Theorem E's classes (P), (Q) and (R) was checked by exact computation on random data, not proved; Theorem E's explicit criteria do not follow from it. The configurations themselves (the “if” half) give, at a candidate, exclusions that are substitutions in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (Roy 1992, Cor. 2). For the conjugation-stable families they are printed configurations: Diaz's Théorème 7(1) (2007) and Théorème 2 (2004); in dimension 4, Théorème 7(1) at $v = 1/(u - a)$.
-- source:
--   Not found in the sources read: the “only if” half, the classification. Theorem F asks the question of Theorem E of the mission's research note on polynomial and Laurent hulls (DiazModulus.laurent_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff, Laurent z) for every z rational in u, and builds on Theorem B (DiazModulus.circle_point_extension_two_by_three_configuration_iff, 10.6), which holds for every complex z. For Laurent z, agreement with Theorem E's classes was checked by exact computation, not proved. Its configurations give, at a candidate, exclusions that are substitutions in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (D. Roy, Matrices whose coefficients are linear forms in logarithms, J. Number Theory 41 (1992), 22–47, Cor. 2). Special cases of the “if” half are printed: in dimension 4 the configuration is G. Diaz, Produits et quotients de combinaisons linéaires de logarithmes de nombres algébriques : conjectures et résultats partiels, J. Théor. Nombres Bordeaux 19 (2007), 373–391, Théorème 7(1) at v = 1/(u − a), with the exclusion in its Corollaire 5(4); for polynomials of degree 2 and 3 in u it is Théorème 7(1); Theorem E's class (Q) is a substitution in G. Diaz, Utilisation de la conjugaison complexe dans l'étude de la transcendance de valeurs de la fonction exponentielle usuelle, J. Théor. Nombres Bordeaux 16 (2004), 535–553, Théorème 2, and in Diaz 2007, Théorème 4(1). Uses DiazModulus.rational_space_two_by_three_configuration_iff, DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_le_adjoin, DiazModulus.conj_hull_finrank_four_two_by_three_configuration_iff and DiazModulus.circle_point_config_card_le_four. R20 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 23 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Definitions.Def_DiazModulus

open Complex ComplexConjugate

namespace DiazModulus

open Polynomial in
theorem rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff (u z : ℂ) (hu : u ∉ Qbar)
    (hρ : IsAlgebraic ℚ (u * conj u)) (hz : z ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin Qbar ({u} : Set ℂ)) :
    (∃ (x : Fin 2 → ℂ) (y : Fin 3 → ℂ), LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) x ∧ LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) y ∧
        ∀ i j, x i * y j ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) ↔
      (Module.finrank (↥Qbar) (Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) = 4 ∧ ∃ a ∈ Qbar, a * conj a = u * conj u ∧
          z ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, (u - a)⁻¹} : Set ℂ)) ∨
      (Module.finrank (↥Qbar) (Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) = 5 ∧
        ((∃ t : Fin 3 → ℂ, LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) t ∧ ∀ j, t j ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) ∧ u * t j ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) ∨ (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u P' * aeval u S₂ / (u * aeval u Q')} : Set ℂ)) ∨
        (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u Q' * (aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ + aeval u P' * aeval u S₂) / (u * aeval u P' ^ 2)} :
            Set ℂ)))) := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
